.TH SAPHIRA-BUILD-MCP 1 "October 2026" "saphira-build-mcp 0.1.0" "Saphira"
.SH NAME
saphira-build-mcp \- Saphira build/package queries and evidence journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-build-mcp --mcp
.br
.B saphira-build-mcp --list-tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-build-mcp
is a local MCP stdio server exposing Saphira package, build-queue,
artifact and Unix-identity state to agents, plus an Egg-local
evidence journal (package notes and policy records). It reads the
builder state: recipes, the APK and repository databases, the build
queue and retained logs. It never builds, signs, publishes,
installs or restarts anything, never executes recipe scripts, and
never opens a network socket. Its only write surface is its own
journal database; there is no recipe, queue, revision, signing,
publication or installation authority.
.PP
With
.B --mcp
it speaks JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout (newline-delimited objects;
LSP Content-Length framing accepted as fallback) and exits on EOF.
With
.B --list-tools
it prints the tools/list document (also the build-time self-check).
.SH TOOLS
Sixteen tools. Fourteen are read-only: package_search,
package_info, package_dependencies, package_why_installed,
package_installed, package_build_status, package_build_history,
package_build_log, package_artifacts, build_queue,
package_identity, package_notes_get, package_policy_status,
package_readiness. Two write only to the journal:
package_notes_add and package_policy_record. Every result ends
with a [src: ...] provenance line naming the files read.
.PP
Policy records pin the revisions they were verified against
(recipe, registry and artifact digests). A record whose pins no
longer match the live state reports STALE; absence of a record
reports UNVERIFIED. Stale evidence is never presented as valid.
.SH JOURNAL
The journal lives in notes.db (live default
/var/lib/saphira-build/notes.db on Egg) and is append-only:
new rows supersede, nothing is updated or deleted. Its tables are
maintained by this program. The database must never be carried in
/recipes except blank and empty.
.PP
Keeper and Homer are backup destinations only. Back up with a
SQLite-safe snapshot (sqlite3 notes.db .backup snapshot.db, which
uses the online backup API) and transfer the completed snapshot
with the existing backup infrastructure. Never copy the live file
while writes may occur, and never use Git for journal sync.
.PP
Journal attribution comes from $SBM_AUTHOR (or the per-call author
field, defaulting to "unspecified"): attribution, not
authentication. The recorder field is MCP clientInfo metadata:
client-reported and unverified.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Data-source paths default to the live system and can be pointed at
fixtures for testing:
.B SBM_RECIPES SBM_QUEUE_DB SBM_REPO_DIR SBM_INCOMING SBM_TSV
.B SBM_PASSWD SBM_GROUP SBM_APKDB SBM_NOTES_DB
.PP
.B SBM_AUTHOR
sets the default journal attribution (a per-call author field
overrides it; "unspecified" when neither is set).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success (server exits 0 on stdin EOF). 1 on internal errors.
2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-build (8)
